WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.857
Magrib smiled when the palace gate opened.

2
00:00:04.858 --> 00:00:09.339
"Choose any new lamp you want, my dear!" he said.

3
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.756
Princess Badra and her attendants were looking down from their window.

4
00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:21.436
The servant took a shiny, new lamp and gave the magician Aladdin’s lamp.

5
00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:23.970
"You must be mad, old man,"

6
00:00:23.971 --> 00:00:27.673
the servant said as she closed the gate.

7
00:00:27.674 --> 00:00:30.959
Magrib hurried away with his treasure.

8
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.693
He could still hear the women laughing, but he didn’t care.

9
00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:38.560
"I have the lamp!"

10
00:00:38.561 --> 00:00:43.038
he cried as he tossed the other new lamps into a ditch.

11
00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:47.649
He ran until he reached a quiet place outside the city walls.

12
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.779
Then he rubbed the old brass lamp.

13
00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.134
The genie appeared wrapped in smoke.

14
00:00:55.135 --> 00:01:02.165
Magrib heard a high and mysterious melody, and fell back in surprise.

15
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:07.793
"Here I am, ready to obey you, master!" said the genie.

16
00:01:07.794 --> 00:01:11.135
Then he looked closely at Magrib.

17
00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:14.060
"Who are you?" he asked.

18
00:01:14.061 --> 00:01:16.910
"I expected someone else."

19
00:01:16.911 --> 00:01:21.670
"I am Magrib," said the magician.

20
00:01:21.671 --> 00:01:25.198
"Well, never mind," said the genie.

21
00:01:25.199 --> 00:01:28.442
He crossed his arms over his chest.

22
00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:31.865
"I am the slave of whoever owns the lamp.

23
00:01:31.866 --> 00:01:34.180
Tell me your wish."

24
00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:38.197
"My wish is simple," whispered Magrib.

25
00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:42.679
"Take me and Aladdin’s palace to Egypt."

26
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.168
"Close your eyes," the genie said.

27
00:01:46.169 --> 00:01:49.623
"When you open them, you will be there."

28
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:56.230
Every morning, the sultan loved to look out his window to see his daughter’s palace.

29
00:01:56.231 --> 00:02:02.305
But on this morning, he looked and saw—nothing!

30
00:02:02.306 --> 00:02:07.492
He rubbed his eyes and blinked, but still he saw nothing.

31
00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:11.082
"Where is the palace?" yelled the sultan.

32
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.672
"Where is my daughter?"

33
00:02:13.673 --> 00:02:17.900
He stared at the spot where the palace had once stood.

34
00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:23.710
"Grand Vizier!" he shouted, and his adviser came running.

35
00:02:23.711 --> 00:02:26.732
"Come to the window," said the sultan.

36
00:02:26.733 --> 00:02:29.216
"What do you see?"

37
00:02:29.217 --> 00:02:33.649
"Nothing, my sultan," said the grand vizier.

38
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.797
"Aladdin’s palace has disappeared."

39
00:02:36.798 --> 00:02:41.411
"Oh, where is my daughter?" cried the sultan.

40
00:02:41.412 --> 00:02:48.780
He started to weep.

41
00:02:48.781 --> 00:02:52.561
"I warned you," said the grand vizier.

42
00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:57.068
"I told you Aladdin’s palace was built by magic!"

43
00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:01.081
Then the sultan flew into a rage.

44
00:03:01.082 --> 00:03:03.609
"Where is Aladdin?"

45
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:08.246
"He has gone hunting," said the grand vizier.

46
00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:12.806
"Bring him to me now!" shouted the sultan.

47
00:03:12.807 --> 00:03:15.738
"I’ll have his head cut off!"

48
00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:21.156
Before the end of that day, the sultan’s army had captured Aladdin.

49
00:03:21.157 --> 00:03:25.979
They put him in chains and dragged him back to the city.

50
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.552
Two of the sultan’s guards brought Aladdin to the royal hall.

51
00:03:30.553 --> 00:03:36.282
They forced him to kneel on the ground as the sultan and the grand vizier entered.

52
00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:39.885
The sultan’s eyes were red from crying.

53
00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:48.292
The grand vizier laughed scornfully at Aladdin.

54
00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:52.732
"What is my crime, great sultan?" shouted Aladdin.

55
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:57.889
"You stole my daughter with magic!" cried the sultan.

56
00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:02.495
"And her palace!" added his adviser.

57
00:04:02.496 --> 00:04:06.221
"I don’t understand," said Aladdin.

58
00:04:06.222 --> 00:04:10.846
"Then I will show you," said the sultan. "Come!"

59
00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:14.048
The guards lifted Aladdin to his feet.

60
00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:18.475
They marched him down the hall, following the sultan to his bedroom.

61
00:04:18.476 --> 00:04:21.563
They brought Aladdin to the window.

62
00:04:21.564 --> 00:04:27.901
"Look! Where is your palace and where is my daughter?" the sultan asked.

63
00:04:27.902 --> 00:04:33.054
Aladdin looked out and saw—nothing.

64
00:04:33.055 --> 00:04:36.283
"I didn’t do this," said Aladdin.

65
00:04:36.284 --> 00:04:41.122
"But give me forty days, and I will find the princess and return her to you."

66
00:04:41.123 --> 00:04:44.130
The sultan tearfully agreed.

67
00:04:44.131 --> 00:04:48.428
"But if you do not come back, I will find you.

68
00:04:48.429 --> 00:04:54.507
Then you will die!"

